WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.071
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:15.124
Unit thirty-four: Want, Need and Would Like. Today you will ask for things and make offers politely.

4
00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:17.995
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:22.247
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:23.829
Want.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:26.979
Want means to wish to have or do something.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:28.759
I want a drink.

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.677
Your turn. Say: Want.

10
00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:35.442
Want.

11
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:36.883
Need.

12
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:40.045
Need means to have to have something.

13
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:41.999
I need some sleep.

14
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:45.224
Your turn. Say: Need.

15
00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:48.859
Need.

16
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:50.478
Would like.

17
00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:53.820
Would like means a polite way to say want.

18
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:55.847
I would like some water.

19
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.021
Your turn. Say: Would like.

20
00:01:01.867 --> 00:01:02.868
Would like.

21
00:01:03.617 --> 00:01:04.629
I'd like.

22
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:07.384
I'd like means I would like.

23
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:09.263
I'd like some tea.

24
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.200
Your turn. Say: I'd like.

25
00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.068
I'd like.

26
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:17.586
Please.

27
00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:21.070
Please means a polite word for requests.

28
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:22.742
Water, please.

29
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.817
Your turn. Say: Please.

30
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:29.470
Please.

31
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:30.916
Offer.

32
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.868
Offer means something that you say you will give or do.

33
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:36.949
Thank you for your offer.

34
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.156
Your turn. Say: Offer.

35
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:43.850
Offer.

36
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:45.571
Request.

37
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.663
Request means a polite way of asking for something.

38
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.994
That is a polite request.

39
00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:55.282
Your turn. Say: Request.

40
00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.216
Request.

41
00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:00.916
Polite.

42
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.079
Polite means showing good manners.

43
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:06.091
He is very polite.

44
00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:09.475
Your turn. Say: Polite.

45
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:13.183
Polite.

46
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.918
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:22.179
Visal, what do you want to drink? Be polite!

48
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:32.730
I would like some water, please. Would like is more polite than want. In a shop or a restaurant, we say I'd like… It sounds kind and respectful.

49
00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:34.992
What about need?

50
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:48.519
Need means we must have something. I need some water. You need to rest. After need and want, we can use a noun or to + verb: I want a drink. I want to drink.

51
00:02:49.617 --> 00:02:51.082
How do we make an offer?

52
00:02:52.183 --> 00:03:01.110
Would you like some tea? Yes, please. No, thank you. We use would you like for a polite offer, and we always answer with please or thank you.

53
00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:03.651
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.596
Grammar focus: Want and need and would like.

55
00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:09.257
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.079
I want a drink.

57
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:13.310
You need to rest.

58
00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:16.251
I would like some water, please.

59
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:24.870
Use want and need with a noun or to + verb. Would like is more polite than want. Make an offer with Would you like…? Answer with please or thank you.

60
00:03:25.617 --> 00:03:28.896
Be careful! Don't say: I want a drink, give me.

61
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.914
Say: I'd like a drink, please.

62
00:03:33.214 --> 00:03:34.935
Use would like to be polite.

63
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:38.119
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:40.097
In a Café.

65
00:03:40.397 --> 00:03:42.875
Good morning. I'd like some tea, please.

66
00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:46.554
Would you like some sugar? No, thank you.

67
00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.775
I need a glass of water because I am hot.

68
00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.604
My friend wants to eat noodles.

69
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.331
Polite words like please and thank you are important.

70
00:03:57.433 --> 00:04:01.458
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.317 --> 00:04:04.119
I blank some water, please.

72
00:04:04.419 --> 00:04:07.828
A, would like. B, like would. C, am like.

73
00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.076
The answer is A: would like.

74
00:04:14.217 --> 00:04:16.161
Would you like some tea? blank

75
00:04:16.461 --> 00:04:20.590
A, Yes, please.. B, Yes, I would like.. C, Yes, you would..

76
00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.388
The answer is A: Yes, please..

77
00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.828
She blank to rest because she is tired.

78
00:04:30.128 --> 00:04:33.944
A, need. B, needs. C, needing.

79
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.221
The answer is B: needs.

80
00:04:40.383 --> 00:04:42.325
Which sentence is more polite?

81
00:04:42.625 --> 00:04:47.172
A, I want a drink.. B, I'd like a drink, please.. C, Give me a drink..

82
00:04:50.733 --> 00:04:53.267
The answer is B: I'd like a drink, please..

83
00:04:54.417 --> 00:04:57.450
According to the reading, what does the writer's friend want?

84
00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.008
A, noodles. B, tea. C, sugar.

85
00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.555
The answer is A: noodles.

86
00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.779
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:11.617 --> 00:05:13.709
Write a polite sentence with 'would like'.

88
00:05:22.517 --> 00:05:23.936
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:24.236 --> 00:05:35.320
I would like a glass of orange juice, please. I use would like because it is more polite than want. In a shop or a café, polite words like please and thank you help me to be friendly.

90
00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.538
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:42.681
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and want and need and would like.

92
00:05:42.981 --> 00:05:46.388
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

93
00:05:46.688 --> 00:05:49.457
See you in Unit thirty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:05:49.757 --> 00:05:52.351
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

